/* Portable JSON format of exam journeys (generated by scripts/sync-references.mjs from the EduBase developer documentation, do not edit) */
export const EDUBASE_REFERENCE_EXAM_JOURNEYS = "# EduBase exam journey format\n\nPortable JSON format of the journeys, used by edubase_get_exam_journey_graph and edubase_put_exam_journey_graph.\n\nThe journeys are exported and imported in a portable JSON format, where the contents are referenced by their identification strings. The format is described by a [JSON Schema](https://www.edubase.net/download:view/exam:journey:schema), and it is the same format the journey editor exports and imports files with.\n\n* *integer* **schema**: version of the format, currently *1*\n* *hash* **settings**: settings of the journey, every key is optional\n    * *string/null* **title**: custom title of the journey (at most 255 characters)\n    * *string/null* **description**: description of the journey (at most 1024 characters)\n    * *integer* **max_visits**: maximum visits of a node by a user, between 1 and 50, loops stop with the *loop-limit* outcome (default: 5)\n        * only the completed visits count, entering a node again after an error, a move or a stop is not a loop, and the manual moves of the educators are never stopped\n    * *boolean* **restartable**: finished journeys can be started again by taking the starting exam again\n    * *boolean* **notify_user**: notify the users when they finish the journey\n    * *list{string}* **educators**: user identification strings of the educators notified by the journey, e.g. about its errors and by the *notify* nodes (at most 10, only the owner and the managers of the starting exam, the owner is notified if none are set)\n* *list* **nodes**: nodes of the journey (at most 200)\n    * *string* **node**: stable key of the node, unique within the journey (1-32 letters, digits, - or _)\n    * *string* **type**: type of the node\n        * steps (the users stay until they complete them): *start* (exactly one, the starting exam itself), *exam*, *class*, *quiz*\n        * decisions and actions (passed instantly): *condition*, *split*, *notify*, *flag*, *mark*\n        * *organizer*: passed instantly, only shapes the edges on the canvas (waypoint)\n        * *wait*: waits before continuing\n        * *gate*: waits for an educator to approve or decline the user on the interface\n        * *end*: finishes the journey\n    * *string/null* **label**: custom title of the node (at most 64 characters)\n    * *hash* **position**: position of the node on the canvas (*x* and *y*), nodes without a position are laid out automatically\n    * *hash* **config**: configuration of the node, depending on its type\n        * *start*: **complete_on** (when the step is completed: *finish* when the exam is finished, *success* when it is finished successfully, *final* when its result is final)\n        * *exam*: **exam** (exam identification string), **complete_on** (see above), **retake** (revisiting the step grants a retake), **reuse** (results achieved before entering the step complete it)\n        * *class*: **class** (class identification string), **reuse** (an earlier completion of the class completes the step on every visit)\n        * *quiz*: **quiz** (Quiz set identification string), **min_result** (minimum result of a play completing the step in percentage), **min_plays** (number of plays needed, between 1 and 100)\n        * *condition*: **branches** (at most 16, evaluated in order, the first matching one is taken, *else* otherwise), each with a **key**, a **label**, a **match** mode (*all* or *any* of the rules) and at most 16 **rules**; **else_label** (label of the *else* output)\n        * *split*: **branches** (at least 2, at most 16) with a **key**, a **label** and a relative **weight** (0-1000) to split the users randomly\n        * *wait*: **mode** and its settings\n            * *duration*: for **minutes** (between 1 and 525600)\n            * *date*: until the **date**, given either as YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM in the **timezone** of the node (the same moment for every user), or as YYYY-MM-DD (the start of that day in the timezone of each user)\n            * *weekday*: until the next **weekday** from 1 (Monday) to 7 (Sunday), at the optional **time** given as HH:MM in the **timezone** of the node, or at the start of that day in the timezone of each user without a time\n            * **timezone**: IANA name like *Europe/Budapest*, used with a date and time or a weekday time (default: UTC)\n        * *notify*: **target** (*user* or *educators*), **message** (at most 500 characters)\n        * *flag*: **name** of the flag to set and its **value** (at most 64 characters)\n        * *mark*: **mode** (*mark* or *unmark* the user on the users page of the starting exam)\n        * *gate*: **notify_educators** (notify the educators of the journey when a user arrives), **notify_user** (notify the user when approved or declined)\n        * *organizer*: **input** and **output** (sides of the input and the output on the canvas: *left*, *top*, *right* or *bottom*, they have to be different, default: *left* and *right*)\n        * *end*: **outcome** of the finished journey (*completed*, *failed*, or any custom text of at most 64 characters, default: *completed*)\n    * *hash* **next**: keys of the nodes following this node, keyed by the outputs of this node\n        * steps have a single *done* output, waits, actions and organizers a single *next* output, conditions have an output for each branch key and an *else* output, splits an output for each branch key, gates an *approved* and a *declined* output, end nodes have no outputs\n        * the output names (*done*, *next*, *else*, *approved* and *declined*) cannot be used as branch keys\n        * an output left out or set to null is unconnected, users taking it finish the journey with the *completed* outcome\n        * the *approved* output of a gate has to be connected, users taking an unconnected *declined* output are stopped with the *declined* outcome (an educator can move or resume them)\n    * *string* **marker**, **title**, *hash* **content**: informative only, ignored by the import\n\nThe rules of the conditions have the following fields:\n\n* *string* **field**: the compared value\n    * the completed step: *step.result*, *step.successful*, *step.grade*, *step.attempts*, *step.time_spent*, *step.visits*, *step.skill*\n    * an earlier node of the journey: *node.result*, *node.successful*, *node.grade*, *node.time_spent*, *node.completed*, *node.visits*, *node.skill*\n    * the user: *exam.custom*, *user.gender*, *user.birthdate*, *user.customer_field*, *user.department*, *user.team*, *user.generated*\n    * the journey and the current date: *journey.flag*, *journey.days*, *journey.steps*, *date.weekday*, *date.hour*, *date.date*, *date.datetime*\n    * results are compared as percentages (0-100)\n* *string* **param**: parameter of the field (at most 64 characters)\n    * needed by *step.skill* (skill identifier), the *node.\\** fields (node key, or node key and skill identifier separated by a colon for *node.skill*), *exam.custom* (exam identification string and field label or hash separated by a colon), *user.customer_field* (name of the field) and *journey.flag* (name of the flag)\n* *string* **operator**: the comparison\n    * possible values: eq / neq / gt / gte / lt / lte / between / elapsed / in / not_in / contains / empty / not_empty / is_true / is_false\n    * *empty*, *not_empty*, *is_true* and *is_false* need no value, *between* needs a [minimum, maximum] list (inclusive), *in* and *not_in* need a list (at most 64 items)\n    * *elapsed* compares the time passed since a date value (e.g. *user.birthdate* or a date custom field with *exam.custom*) at the time of the decision with a [minimum, maximum] list of whole *unit*s (inclusive, one of the limits can be null, future dates give negative values)\n* *mixed* **value**: value to compare with\n    * dates are YYYY-MM-DD calendar days and are never converted (*date.date* is the current day of the user)\n    * date and time values are YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM, in UTC for *exam.custom* (*datetime* custom fields are stored in UTC, and compared by the day of the user when the rule has dates), and in the timezone of the rule for *date.datetime*\n    * a *between* range has to use the same kind of value for both limits (two dates, or two date and time values)\n    * departments are given by their titles, teams by their identification strings\n* *string* **aggregate**: which completion of an earlier node is compared (*node.\\** fields, except *node.completed* and *node.visits*)\n    * possible values: last / first / best / worst / average\n    * default: last\n* *string* **measure**: whether the collected points or the percentage of the maximum is compared (skill fields)\n    * possible values: points / percent\n    * default: points\n* *string* **unit**: unit of the *elapsed* operator (mandatory for it)\n    * possible values: years / months / weeks / days / hours / minutes\n    * completed units are counted, so the *years* since a birth date are the age of the user\n    * dates without a time are calendar days of the user, and they are counted until the current day of the user\n* *string* **time**: the rule only matches on the listed days from this time on, given as HH:MM (*date.weekday* only, optional)\n* *string* **timezone**: timezone the rule is evaluated in (IANA name like *Europe/Budapest*)\n    * used by *date.hour*, *date.datetime*, and *date.weekday* with a *time*, the other date fields use the timezone of the user\n    * default: UTC\n";
